{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1106054-dragon-blooded-charm-preview-signature-charms","id":1106054,"title":"Dragon-Blooded Charm preview - Signature Charms","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-21T07:55:59-07:00","id":1106054,"title":"Dragon-Blooded Charm preview - Signature Charms","content":"Latest DB Charm preview now up, introducing Signature Charms: <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/signature-charms-dragon-blooded-pt-3-exalted/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/signature-cha...-pt-3-exalted/</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T08:41:20-07:00","id":1106074,"title":"","content":"Signature charms are interesting, I thought Wildfire-Taming Technique was rather weak until I realised there's no restriction on the Dragon Blooded setting the fire themselves.<br /> <br /> Even just beating the threshold means that all your enemies are taking environment penalties, and you can use it as cover.<br /> <br /> Does &quot;the Exalt and her companions&quot; also apply to any mortals they have with them? If they have any army? If her companions split up significantly?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1794-doran","name":"doran","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1794_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T09:13:24-07:00","id":1106082,"title":"","content":"Hmm, this will make E3 a pretty big jump in power. No prereqs means you can pick up a couple quickly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Some of me humble homebrew for ex3:<br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hOOjEGyoq3owLoUwIwTfWKTffzo_udsiUTwomw7wudA/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Artifacts for Crumple's DB homebrew</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1tI2T1Re0G8QOuoXkH7Y4PrKQxk1BPEGpbi82SpkTyIw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Some Lintha QCs</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1O2I_2iWTCflJ36ggkDvjTeXmzFsGHKRxAi6L_Ry6g4w/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A Wyld Behemoth</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8838-tds","name":"TDS","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T09:17:55-07:00","id":1106089,"title":"","content":"The wildfire ignores you and your companions for a story? That seems really long.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4915-darkuwa","name":"Darkuwa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4915_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T09:22:57-07:00","id":1106094,"title":"","content":"I was pretty unhappy with the idea that learning one Signature Charm for an Ability locks you out of the others, until I made myself think of it like <i><u>RWBY </u></i>Semblances. Rather than &quot;I learn this one trick, and now my brain is too full&quot; it is more like &quot;I learned this one trick because it was the one trick I could learn; this is the trick which was within my personal nature.&quot;<br /> <br /> All five of these Charms are badass.<br /> <br /> The Wood-aspected Larceny Charm makes me think of <i>Majora's Mask</i>, but also that one part in <i>Okami </i>where you infiltrate the island of demons by making your own rice-paper-and-ink-marking mask to pose as a demon. I suppose it could also evoke <i>Team Fortress II's</i> Spy class.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T09:37:15-07:00","id":1106101,"title":"","content":"I like anything that creates a gap between Dragon-Blooded PCs and major NPCs from their immediate peers without resorting to a mountain of XP.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T09:38:18-07:00","id":1106102,"title":"","content":"The charms are pretty cool. I quite like the intent of them being, well, signature tricks at the heart of each Dragon-Blooded ability charmset with few prerequisites that you can learn as suits your elemental preference. Between the unrevealed details of Elemental Aura and favored costs, you'll probably have enough encouragement to pick the one that matches your element or the aspect favoring that ability, but the flexibility is good.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure about each signature charm pick locking you out of four potential others. Personally not bothered by it at all and I appreciate how it can distinguish Dragon-Blooded characters, but it might be easy for some perspectives to take umbrage at it as restrictive design.<br /> <br /> Most of them having no prerequisites (except the Bureaucracy one because I would assume it shares the &quot;main&quot; element of its ability set) reflects well on their accessibility, and all the charms shown are definitely impressive or stylish in their context.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 06-21-2017, 01:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T09:40:08-07:00","id":1106104,"title":"","content":"Extremely neat stuff. I'm getting more and more stoked for What Fire Has Wrought every time we see something new.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T09:45:38-07:00","id":1106106,"title":"","content":"Neat.<br /> <br /> \u200bI'm guessing that Signature Charms aren't limited to Aspect element, so it creates an interesting new dimension to the elemental qualities of the Dragon Blooded. Like, War isn't an Aspect Ability of Wood, but there's a signature Wood power for your Tepet Ejava in there to mean that she can still express her own elemental nature through one of her most important Abilities. Alternatively, you could have a Wood Aspect who focuses on the Aspect Abilities and plays into one of the more iconic roles of the Aspect like a ranger, but can express iconic powers to exert themselves over a number of elements in expression of that role.<br /> <br /> \u200bI mean, elemental Charms and aura already afford certain diversity, but the idea of certain iconic Charms seems like a particularly focused presentation of either possibility.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T10:08:10-07:00","id":1106114,"title":"","content":"...okay, Wyld Hunts are gonna be A LOT scarier in this edition.<br /> <br /> Distraction of the Babbling Brook is really solid for socialites...ESPECIALLY in conjunction with the Eclipse Oath. Good way to turn the powers of the Anathema against them, or provide still-useful backup in a mixed party.<br /> <br /> Sleeping Dragon's Lair...eh, I'm less excited about it, but it's cool for ninja-type characters. It'd pair well with Ebon Shadow Style, for instance...and after the first Dragonblooded ambush by a Wyld Hunt using this charm, PCs are gonna be scared of dirt, which I kind of love.<br /> <br /> Tempest Ruling Commander is my new favorite charm. I've been wanting &quot;War Weather&quot; as described in earlier editions for ages. Enough said.<br /> <br /> Terrifying Forest Devil Mask...let's you play Zuko pretending to be the Blue Spirit! And lets you play Dragonblooded Batman! And lets you play the White Plains Rider from the quest right here on the forums! It's an excellent charm and I love it.<br /> <br /> Wildfire Taming Technique...I didn't love at first. But then I realized I love it. Imagine being HUNTED by a five-mile wide inferno. And the Wyld Hunt following it can walk through it completely unharmed. And if you flee to civilization where it doesn't work...well, the Dragonbloods kind of RUN civilization. This charm feels like the result of a thousand years of war between the Dragonblooded and the Lunar Anathema, and it makes them feel like Princes of the Earth if they're using it as PCs but it's also a great &quot;bad guy&quot; power for when you want to portray a villain not caring about the destruction he causes to try and get to his nemesis. Lots of story potential here!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T10:45:57-07:00","id":1106138,"title":"","content":"Have I understood correctly... that there are 125 signature charms in the book? 5 for each ability?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T10:49:56-07:00","id":1106140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1106054-dragon-blooded-charm-preview-signature-charms?p=1106106#post1106106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Neat.<br /> <br /> \u200bI'm guessing that Signature Charms aren't limited to Aspect element, so it creates an interesting new dimension to the elemental qualities of the Dragon Blooded. Like, War isn't an Aspect Ability of Wood, but there's a signature Wood power for your Tepet Ejava in there to mean that she can still express her own elemental nature through one of her most important Abilities. Alternatively, you could have a Wood Aspect who focuses on the Aspect Abilities and plays into one of the more iconic roles of the Aspect like a ranger, but can express iconic powers to exert themselves over a number of elements in expression of that role.<br /> <br /> \u200bI mean, elemental Charms and aura already afford certain diversity, but the idea of certain iconic Charms seems like a particularly focused presentation of either possibility.</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume that's part of the point. That whereas before, the Fire-aspected great general and the Air-aspected great general fought in pretty much the same way (as we found) whereas now, they'll be distinct, as &quot;All the war charms&quot; for Air and &quot;all the War charms&quot; for Fire, are not the same thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T11:06:07-07:00","id":1106150,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the preview says that there's one signature charm of each element for each ability. Presumably you don't <i>have</i> to pick the one that matches your aspect, but I suspect a lot of people will. <br /> <br /> Still no idea how Aura gets activated or what benefits matching it to your aspect has though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T11:11:59-07:00","id":1106153,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'm still hoping to hear about that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T12:09:37-07:00","id":1106188,"title":"","content":"I guess I have a question (constructive criticism!) about the concept, just around custom Charms.<br /> <br /> With the Signature Charms as I understand them from the preview, I guess an implication would be that, if they are an open set... then if you go out and write a bunch of Signature Charms, then that means implicitly that you should't go and write a bunch of E5 Charms that do mechanically similar things. As the Essence 3 Signature Charm gets larger, then the Essence 5 Charm selection gets smaller. If so, I'm not sure how good an idea it feels to introduce that kind of extra complexity into custom Charms. <br /> <br /> This kind of thing wouldn't play if there was a sense in which the Signature Charms were distinct from general higher essence Charms. <br /> <br /> Alternatively, and this is probably more accurate to &quot;each Dragon-Blooded Ability has five powerful Signature Charms, one for each element&quot;, they are finite and all written by developers and you can't Custom them. But then from that angle, that's kind of restricting homebrew to define characters. It's also restricting the ability of the developers as writers to come up with as many Signature Charms as feels right rather than necessarily five per Ability.<br /> <br /> Essentially, I guess, summed up, like, why this rather than; &quot;At Essence 3 you can buy one Essence 5 Charm in each Ability&quot;? That would seem like it has fewer restrictions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T12:26:55-07:00","id":1106197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1106054-dragon-blooded-charm-preview-signature-charms?p=1106188#post1106188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">if you go out and write a bunch of Signature Charms, then that means implicitly that you should't go and write a bunch of E5 Charms that do mechanically similar things. As the Essence 3 Signature Charm gets larger, then the Essence 5 Charm selection gets smaller.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is kind of a confusing conclusion to me. If they weren't called &quot;signature charms&quot; this idea could still stand. Why would you ever write an essence 5 charms that's similar to an essence 3 charm? I'm curious if you can expand on this because despite several paragraphs I'm struggling with how this is suppressing creative space.<br /> <br /> That aside, I'm pretty sure charmsets, while open, aren't designed with empty space for custom charms intentionally. There may be empty space or room to grow, but I doubt it's intentionally dodged for the sake of homebrewers. I assume their goal is to make as complete a charmset as is reasonable and let people decide what they want to fill in.<br /> <br /> That's an assumption on my part, but it seems logical to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T12:45:26-07:00","id":1106201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1106054-dragon-blooded-charm-preview-signature-charms?p=1106188#post1106188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alternatively, and this is probably more accurate to &quot;each Dragon-Blooded Ability has five powerful Signature Charms, one for each element&quot;, they are finite and all written by developers and you can't Custom them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not? It is, as you said, an open charmset. What's to stop you from going to your ST and saying, &quot;Hey, I have a cool idea for an alternate Air-Sail signature charm, because I don't think the one in the book really fits my character&quot;? There's one signature per aspect per ability that's published, but that doesn't mean homebrew can't add to that, if your group is so inclined. In fact, with over a hundred examples to look at, homebrewers should have a very strong grasp of an appropriate power level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10995-abakus","name":"Abakus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T12:52:19-07:00","id":1106208,"title":"","content":"I don't think anyone is going to kill you if you write more signature charms for an Ability. Either way you can still only take one so that problem solves itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T13:05:02-07:00","id":1106218,"title":"","content":"Distraction of the Babbling Brook and Sleeping Dragon's Lair are pretty good charms, though I'm not really sure why they needed to be Signature-keyed. The other three charms, though...oh man. Ohhhh, man. Cool as all hell and all things I wanna take on a character of some sort.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Won't you believe in him? Even if there is no God, or Buddha...there is still Kamen Rider.&quot; \u2014Taki Kazuya, <i>Kamen Rider SPIRITS</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\">Now...count up </span><span style=\"color:#4B0082\">all your sins.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/160-cyclonejoker","name":"CycloneJoker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar160_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T13:18:57-07:00","id":1106225,"title":"","content":"In short, here were my immediate sound-bite reactions to the previewed charms.<br /> <br /> <b>Distraction of the Babbling Brook</b> - Huh, handy.<br /> <br /> <b>Sleeping Dragon's Lair</b> - Earth Aspects vanishing into ground. That's pretty cool.<br /> <br /> <b>Tempest-Ruling Commander</b> - A general bending the skies to their will? Okay, <i>awesome</i>.<br /> <br /> <b>Terrifying Forest-Devil Mask</b> - ... I can think of like three character concepts based on this charm <i>alone</i>.<br /> <br /> <b>Wildfire-Taming Technique</b> - Dude, <i>holy shit</i>. *Reads the post someone else made about how it doesn't say the DB can't START a forest fire and use this Charm on it* ... Dude. <i>DUUUUUUUUUUUDE</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T13:52:20-07:00","id":1106240,"title":"","content":"Distraction of the Babbling Brook- A lawyer wrote a lawyer charm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T13:57:37-07:00","id":1106245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1106054-dragon-blooded-charm-preview-signature-charms?p=1106114#post1106114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Distraction of the Babbling Brook is really solid for socialites...ESPECIALLY in conjunction with the Eclipse Oath. Good way to turn the powers of the Anathema against them, or provide still-useful backup in a mixed party.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this meme relevant?<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://ep60qmdjq8-flywheel.netdna-ssl.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/02/khaled.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T14:32:25-07:00","id":1106260,"title":"","content":"I wish I wasn't so obsessed with Lunars. I'd be ready to make the Dragon-Blooded my new favorites.<br /> <br /> I've long thought that the Dragon-Blooded were interesting enough to replace the Solar Exalted as the main splat of the game, and Third Edition seems posed to finally back their concept up with the mechanics that earlier developers just didn't have the experience to attempt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T14:52:09-07:00","id":1106268,"title":"","content":"The very fact that the wildfire charm says it doesn't care if a solar is using Traceless Passage, well that just makes me happy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1777-kell_tamer","name":"Kell_Tamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1777_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T14:58:57-07:00","id":1106271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1106054-dragon-blooded-charm-preview-signature-charms?p=1106197#post1106197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is kind of a confusing conclusion to me. If they weren't called &quot;signature charms&quot; this idea could still stand. Why would you ever write an essence 5 charms that's similar to an essence 3 charm? I'm curious if you can expand on this because despite several paragraphs I'm struggling with how this is suppressing creative space.<br /> <br /> That aside, I'm pretty sure charmsets, while open, aren't designed with empty space for custom charms intentionally. There may be empty space or room to grow, but I doubt it's intentionally dodged for the sake of homebrewers. I assume their goal is to make as complete a charmset as is reasonable and let people decide what they want to fill in.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm thinking you would write a Essence 5 non-Sig DB Charm that is similar to an Essence 3 Sig DB Charm, as E3 Sig seem supposed to be extra strong for their level, so I would have thought functionally more equivalent to a higher Essence Charm. Then there would be some inevitable overlapping between what E3 Sig and higher Essence non-Sig are doing. This could be wrong, but from the preview I don't totally know why, exactly.<br /> <br /> It's not so much that I'm thinking that Charms would be designed with empty space as such, in the sense of intentionally leaving gaps to fill. It's that I would expect that Charmsets would be designed with the expectation that people will homebrew, and then with that in mind, to simplify the decision process of homebrew as much as possible. Considerations like &quot;If I design this higher Essence Charm that is functionally equivalent to a lower Essence Signature Charm, will I be undermining what Signature Charms are meant to achieve? Will my ST not allow it because he's not sure if it's undermining what Signature Charms are meant to achieve?&quot; seem like they add overhead there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T15:23:24-07:00","id":1106285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1106054-dragon-blooded-charm-preview-signature-charms?p=1106271#post1106271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm thinking you would write a Essence 5 non-Sig DB Charm that is similar to an Essence 3 Sig DB Charm, as E3 Sig seem supposed to be extra strong for their level, so I would have thought functionally more equivalent to a higher Essence Charm. Then there would be some inevitable overlapping between what E3 Sig and higher Essence non-Sig are doing. This could be wrong, but from the preview I don't totally know why, exactly.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is clearer though I don't have that fear. Remember that not even every charm tree for Solars even <b>had</b> Essence 5 charms. But they all go to Essence 3. Vance has gone on record to say that he never approaches charm design based on &quot;hmm what would make a good Essence X charm&quot; but instead comes up with the charm concept first and then figures out how strong it seems and applies an Essence level to it. With this approach in mind, it's fair to think that we could still see some trees that don't uniformly go to Essence 5. This design allows every ability to have powerful options available.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1106054-dragon-blooded-charm-preview-signature-charms?p=1106271#post1106271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not so much that I'm thinking that Charms would be designed with empty space as such, in the sense of intentionally leaving gaps to fill. It's that I would expect that Charmsets would be designed with the expectation that people will homebrew, and then with that in mind, to simplify the decision process of homebrew as much as possible. Considerations like &quot;If I design this higher Essence Charm that is functionally equivalent to a lower Essence Signature Charm, will I be undermining what Signature Charms are meant to achieve? Will my ST not allow it because he's not sure if it's undermining what Signature Charms are meant to achieve?&quot; seem like they add overhead there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hear you, but I just don't think that is how they do it. Since there's no basis for either of our theories, so it's just theories, but I don't think those are considerations the writers take into account when designing. Like at all. <br /> <br /> As has been said above, since you can only take 1 Signature Charm per Ability, I don't see anything wrong with you homebrewing different Signature charms. Whether it's &quot;allowed&quot; by your ST is up to your ST, not the devs. That has been the drum they constantly beat this edition.<br /> <br /> My 2 cents. Thanks for clarifying your position for me!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T15:32:46-07:00","id":1106292,"title":"","content":"I was hoping there would be clearer delineation of fluff and mechanics in the DB book. The rules seem a little clearer than the core though.<br /> If every charm is so lengthy just how big of a book are we talking here? As big as the EX3 core?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/977-major","name":"Major","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar977_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T16:15:41-07:00","id":1106310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Major</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1106054-dragon-blooded-charm-preview-signature-charms?p=1106292#post1106292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was hoping there would be clearer delineation of fluff and mechanics in the DB book. The rules seem a little clearer than the core though.<br /> If every charm is so lengthy just how big of a book are we talking here? As big as the EX3 core?</div> </div> </div> </div>Certainly not that big. Core book had to cover base game, which will already be established for the DB book. Core book covered basic mechanics, both combat, social, craft, sorcery, and others, the basics of artifacts and hearthstones, and the geography of all of Creation, none of which needs to be covered in the DB book. Additionally, not all of the charms that have been previewed have been that long, and Vance also said that the number of charms is smaller than the Solar tree, like a little more than half if I recall correctly (which I could be wrong).<br /> <br /> The book will be smaller.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T16:39:08-07:00","id":1106318,"title":"","content":"Bear in mind, the core book describes essence 5 as &quot;vanishingly rare&quot; among dragon blooded. Since they have no supernal equivalent it makes sense that essence 5 charms would be rare and that any big flashy effects that could be called &quot;signature&quot; would need to be at lower essence requirement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T19:13:17-07:00","id":1106372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1106054-dragon-blooded-charm-preview-signature-charms?p=1106138#post1106138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have I understood correctly... that there are 125 signature charms in the book? 5 for each ability?</div> </div> </div> </div>For comparison's sake, 2e had only about twice that many DB Charms total (about 264, if my tally is accurate). That's gonna be a <i>lot</i> of new Charms.<br /> <br /> These are fun! I'm having trouble following some of the thematic associations that go from &quot;Wood-Aspected Elemental soldier&quot; to Mamoru Chiba, but I can think of so many character concepts that would use that Charm I almost don't care.<br /> <br /> Tempest-Ruling Commander is really cool, but am I reading right that you'd have to beat the opposing commander's roll by five successes to get any utility out of it? That seems like a pretty steep hill to climb given limited DB dice pools - it seems almost like the only times you'd be likely to use it would be against enemies who are so bad at mass combat you don't <i>need</i> to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T20:35:46-07:00","id":1106393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1106054-dragon-blooded-charm-preview-signature-charms?p=1106372#post1106372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tempest-Ruling Commander is really cool, but am I reading right that you'd have to beat the opposing commander's roll by five successes to get any utility out of it? That seems like a pretty steep hill to climb given limited DB dice pools - it seems almost like the only times you'd be likely to use it would be against enemies who are so bad at mass combat you don't <i>need</i> to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, they may not be able to use it against Solar!Sun Tzu, but the Wyld hunt will still spend plenty of time chasing down Anathema who aren't invested in War but are still dangerous enough you'll want every edge you can get like your stereotypical swordmaster Dawn, underworld necromancer, or infernalist cult with summoned demons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11796-sergregness","name":"serGregness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11796_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T20:43:37-07:00","id":1106395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1106054-dragon-blooded-charm-preview-signature-charms?p=1106372#post1106372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tempest-Ruling Commander is really cool, but am I reading right that you'd have to beat the opposing commander's roll by five successes to get any utility out of it? That seems like a pretty steep hill to climb given limited DB dice pools - it seems almost like the only times you'd be likely to use it would be against enemies who are so bad at mass combat you don't <i>need</i> to.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>serGregness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1106054-dragon-blooded-charm-preview-signature-charms?p=1106393#post1106393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, they may not be able to use it against Solar!Sun Tzu, but the Wyld hunt will still spend plenty of time chasing down Anathema who aren't invested in War but are still dangerous enough you'll want every edge you can get like your stereotypical swordmaster Dawn, underworld necromancer, or infernalist cult with summoned demons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Signature Charms <i>might</i> actually be Signature Charm-<i>cascades</i>, with various upgrades or advanced tricks leading up from them.<br /> <br /> What I'm saying is that another Charm could make it possible to get some use out of TRC even without beating a Solar general's roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T21:16:26-07:00","id":1106402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>serGregness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1106054-dragon-blooded-charm-preview-signature-charms?p=1106393#post1106393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, they may not be able to use it against Solar!Sun Tzu, but the Wyld hunt will still spend plenty of time chasing down Anathema who aren't invested in War but are still dangerous enough you'll want every edge you can get like your stereotypical swordmaster Dawn, underworld necromancer, or infernalist cult with summoned demons.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, I think we can safely take Solar Sun Tzu off the table here. You don't just need to roll five successes - you need to roll five <i>more</i> successes than the other guy rolled. Unless DB pools are a lot bigger than they were in 2e, that's going to be uncommon even against competent mortal opposition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T01:21:13-07:00","id":1106444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1106054-dragon-blooded-charm-preview-signature-charms?p=1106372#post1106372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm having trouble following some of the thematic associations that go from &quot;Wood-Aspected Elemental soldier&quot; to Mamoru Chiba</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI think that there's a certain shamanic association with the Wood Aspect, something that could be seen in some of the archetypes featured in their Aspect Book.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt reminds me a bit of Tepet Ejava's Exaltation story, which if I recall happened under circumstances that had her briefly fear that she had actually become a Lunar.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T01:31:38-07:00","id":1106445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1106054-dragon-blooded-charm-preview-signature-charms?p=1106402#post1106402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, I think we can safely take Solar Sun Tzu off the table here. You don't just need to roll five successes - you need to roll five <i>more</i> successes than the other guy rolled. Unless DB pools are a lot bigger than they were in 2e, that's going to be uncommon even against competent mortal opposition.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, less likely than I think you're expecting for the kind of character who even <i>takes</i> a Signature charm in War to begin with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11796-sergregness","name":"serGregness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11796_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T02:02:12-07:00","id":1106451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1106054-dragon-blooded-charm-preview-signature-charms?p=1106402#post1106402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, I think we can safely take Solar Sun Tzu off the table here. You don't just need to roll five successes - you need to roll five <i>more</i> successes than the other guy rolled. Unless DB pools are a lot bigger than they were in 2e, that's going to be uncommon even against competent mortal opposition.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, even if we disregarded the dicepool issue, Solar Sun Tzu has a War Charm that just lets him effortlessly negate any kind of magical Strategem. Solars basically autowin Strategic Warfare with enough investment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Some of me humble homebrew for ex3:<br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hOOjEGyoq3owLoUwIwTfWKTffzo_udsiUTwomw7wudA/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Artifacts for Crumple's DB homebrew</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1tI2T1Re0G8QOuoXkH7Y4PrKQxk1BPEGpbi82SpkTyIw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Some Lintha QCs</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1O2I_2iWTCflJ36ggkDvjTeXmzFsGHKRxAi6L_Ry6g4w/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A Wyld Behemoth</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8838-tds","name":"TDS","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T06:33:57-07:00","id":1106516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TDS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1106054-dragon-blooded-charm-preview-signature-charms?p=1106451#post1106451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, even if we disregarded the dicepool issue, Solar Sun Tzu has a War Charm that just lets him effortlessly negate any kind of magical Strategem. Solars basically autowin Strategic Warfare with enough investment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, I don't think he's a useful point of comparison. I do think &quot;mortal with an eight-die pool&quot; is one, and that guy would still be pretty tough to get a +5 success advantage against. (AnyDice suggests that even if you're throwing 15 dice around yourself, you have a &lt;40% chance of the Charm firing.)<br /> <br /> I'm not calling it impossible or useless - just, if I had a player purchasing this, I might want to forewarn them that it's going to be impressive <i>when</i> it fires, but they shouldn't count on that happening.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>serGregness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1106054-dragon-blooded-charm-preview-signature-charms?p=1106445#post1106445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, less likely than I think you're expecting for the kind of character who even <i>takes</i> a Signature charm in War to begin with.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm having trouble parsing this - can you try me again?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T06:45:48-07:00","id":1106522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1106054-dragon-blooded-charm-preview-signature-charms?p=1106516#post1106516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right, I don't think he's a useful point of comparison. I do think &quot;mortal with an eight-die pool&quot; is one, and that guy would still be pretty tough to get a +5 success advantage against. (AnyDice suggests that even if you're throwing 15 dice around yourself, you have a &lt;40% chance of the Charm firing.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think the dragon-blooded will be entirely out in the cold when it comes to dietricks, fwiw.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11456-nihnoz","name":"nihnoz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11456_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T06:57:18-07:00","id":1106528,"title":"","content":"Aren't their pseudo-excellencies supposed to get a bit extra to justify having to buy them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T07:31:11-07:00","id":1106537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1106054-dragon-blooded-charm-preview-signature-charms?p=1106528#post1106528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aren't their pseudo-excellencies supposed to get a bit extra to justify having to buy them?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a great reminder folks. DBs are getting unique die tricks across abilities, not universal excellencies. We don't know what War's tricks will be, but the hope is that Vance takes that into account when designing his rules like that in Tempest-Ruling Commander.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T07:42:45-07:00","id":1106541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1106054-dragon-blooded-charm-preview-signature-charms?p=1106516#post1106516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm having trouble parsing this - can you try me again?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. What I'm trying to say is that the kind of character who takes a Signature charm in War <i>usually</i> is also the kind of character who's also rocking a bunch of other War charms to give them the threshold they need. Said another way, the kind of character who picks up this charm as a payoff to winning strategic warfare is probably also going to invest in setting up that strategic warfare victory in the first place.<br /> <br /> Not to mention, if you keep in mind the reset condition on Tempest-Ruling Commander, charm interactions with the strategic warfare dice modifiers might be a significant theme of the DB war set, in which case 15 dice might not even be the cap for a DB general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11796-sergregness","name":"serGregness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11796_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T08:04:59-07:00","id":1106551,"title":"","content":"One thing I'm a bit uncertain about is the War Charm. I know there's been a desire to reduce the degree to which Charms can substitute for sorcery in the past, and this is an example that I'm worried might be a bit borderline, at best.<br /> <br /> That it functions using stratagem mechanics placates that a bit, but I'm still wary.<br /> <br /> Also, should this be a place to point out a few technical errors?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T09:24:29-07:00","id":1106606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kell_Tamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1106054-dragon-blooded-charm-preview-signature-charms?p=1106268#post1106268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The very fact that the wildfire charm says it doesn't care if a solar is using Traceless Passage, well that just makes me happy.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, the DB still has to get threshold successes (past the fire taming requirements) such that they can beat a solar's Wits+Survival roll with double 9's <i>and</i> Essence auto Sux. I think this is basically just calling out the fact that this counts as magical tracking for purposes of Traceless Passage.<br /> <br /> That said, I still think this charm is really cool! I love that you can send out a forest fire as a bloodhound.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T09:40:25-07:00","id":1106620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1106054-dragon-blooded-charm-preview-signature-charms?p=1106606#post1106606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, the DB still has to get threshold successes (past the fire taming requirements) such that they can beat a solar's Wits+Survival roll with double 9's <i>and</i> Essence auto Sux. I think this is basically just calling out the fact that this counts as magical tracking for purposes of Traceless Passage.<br /> <br /> That said, I still think this charm is really cool! I love that you can send out a forest fire as a bloodhound.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah I know, but the fact the charm doesn't say &quot;This fails against charms of celestial exalted&quot; like a LOT of 2e stuff did, that makes me happy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1777-kell_tamer","name":"Kell_Tamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1777_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T10:37:59-07:00","id":1106634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1106054-dragon-blooded-charm-preview-signature-charms?p=1106537#post1106537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is a great reminder folks. DBs are getting unique die tricks across abilities, not universal excellencies. We don't know what War's tricks will be, but the hope is that Vance takes that into account when designing his rules like that in Tempest-Ruling Commander.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, this is fair. I'm just registering it as a &quot;Hm&quot; from the little we know so far - the big picture may change any number of things.<br /> <br /> Again, to reiterate, these look like fun!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T10:47:41-07:00","id":1106640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1106054-dragon-blooded-charm-preview-signature-charms?p=1106551#post1106551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, should this be a place to point out a few technical errors?</div> </div> </div> </div>The preview Charms haven't been subject to my own editing passes, redlining by Eric, or editing. I do try to take feedback into account, but pointing out technical errors probably isn't the best use of your time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T10:52:26-07:00","id":1106642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1106054-dragon-blooded-charm-preview-signature-charms?p=1106640#post1106640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do try to take feedback into account, but pointing out technical errors probably isn't the best use of your time.</div> </div> </div> </div>What <i>is</i> the best use of our time?<br /> <br /> (I hope it's &quot;getting jazzed for Dragon-Blooded!&quot;)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T11:06:04-07:00","id":1106648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1106054-dragon-blooded-charm-preview-signature-charms?p=1106634#post1106634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, this is fair. I'm just registering it as a &quot;Hm&quot; from the little we know so far - the big picture may change any number of things.<br /> <br /> Again, to reiterate, these look like fun!</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a great thing to point out, because it's a valid problem if it's NOT taken into account when designing the charm and dice tricks. I'm probably just twitchy when I see conversations even vaguely drift in the direction of &quot;I see possible loophole X in the future and that's going to make this terribad!&quot; I get that's not your point, so I may have overkilled my response a bit. ^_^;;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T11:40:47-07:00","id":1106663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1106054-dragon-blooded-charm-preview-signature-charms?p=1106648#post1106648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a great thing to point out, because it's a valid problem if it's NOT taken into account when designing the charm and dice tricks. I'm probably just twitchy when I see conversations even vaguely drift in the direction of &quot;I see possible loophole X in the future and that's going to make this terribad!&quot; I get that's not your point, so I may have overkilled my response a bit. ^_^;;</div> </div> </div> </div>I can understand that impulse. Remember when the devs revealed that the Dragon Styles wouldn't have the Mastery keyword? I remember someone in that thread who was convinced that this made the Dragon Styles a sucker's choice for Solars just because they can't get more out of the Dragon Style individual charms than a Dragonblood.<br /> <br /> I think they were using phrases like 'a trap for Solars', implying that learning a Dragon Style is just a waste of XP for Solars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T12:35:42-07:00","id":1106696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1106054-dragon-blooded-charm-preview-signature-charms?p=1106642#post1106642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What <i>is</i> the best use of our time?<br /> <br /> (I hope it's &quot;getting jazzed for Dragon-Blooded!&quot;)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm a developer, not a philosopher!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T13:01:54-07:00","id":1106705,"title":"","content":"Signature charms are something I'm really excited for, because they look spectacularly easy to homebrew compared to something like a martial art, or a new charm branch leading up to what you actually want. Ability 5, Essence 3, few or no prerequisites, it can be slightly overtuned, it can have a ton of different effects (players tend to homebrew really complicated charm effects), and that's all fine, it's all fine, whereas with most charms you need to kind of keep all that in mind and balance them all. It also comes at Essence 3, right when you're comfortable with the systems at play and comfortable with your character. I love them!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11456-nihnoz","name":"nihnoz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11456_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T13:12:38-07:00","id":1106708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1106054-dragon-blooded-charm-preview-signature-charms?p=1106663#post1106663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can understand that impulse. Remember when the devs revealed that the Dragon Styles wouldn't have the Mastery keyword? I remember someone in that thread who was convinced that this made the Dragon Styles a sucker's choice for Solars just because they can't get more out of the Dragon Style individual charms than a Dragonblood.<br /> <br /> I think they were using phrases like 'a trap for Solars', implying that learning a Dragon Style is just a waste of XP for Solars.</div> </div> </div> </div>Conditionally. It could also make any other Dragon-Blooded combat build a sucker's choice. I continue to grant that there may be unforeseen balancing factors, but those keywords are crucial in Martial Arts balance as we know it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T13:33:01-07:00","id":1106712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Storyteller decides the fire\u2019s speed based on the environs and weather, up to a maximum of <b>150 miles per hour in ideal conditions</b>. However, if there is no path of forested land, grass, peat, or other fuel that the fire can follow to pursue its target, its efforts end, making it possible to escape by fleeing from the wilderness.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>...Ooookay. So, if I went out to the dry prairie during summertime, I could incinerate everything that lived there in a matter of minutes? Or does the fire get to racing speed <i>only </i>if you have it follow somebody?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T17:00:21-07:00","id":1106787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1106054-dragon-blooded-charm-preview-signature-charms?p=1106138#post1106138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have I understood correctly... that there are 125 signature charms in the book? 5 for each ability?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I got out of it. That would take up a huge percentage of the book, none of these are small charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T11:17:55-07:00","id":1107068,"title":"","content":"Indeed, that's what I was wondering about. (Though the charms we see may be longer than average, because posting the charm that says &quot;You can get double 8s on craft rolls when working in a team with other DBs&quot; is not going to inspire people to buy the book as much as a charm about, say, attacking people with a tentacle of water summoned from the nearby river).<br /> <br /> I note that Vance has, in the other thread, said that you can indeed buy signature charms out-of-aspect. So, even if half the charms are signature charms, it's not so limiting.<br /> Can anyone remind me how many Solar charms there were in the Core?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T11:37:48-07:00","id":1107075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1106054-dragon-blooded-charm-preview-signature-charms?p=1107068#post1107068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can anyone remind me how many Solar charms there were in the Core?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm gonna say somewhere in the area of six hundred.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T12:29:36-07:00","id":1107088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1106054-dragon-blooded-charm-preview-signature-charms?p=1107068#post1107068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can anyone remind me how many Solar charms there were in the Core?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just did a quick count and there are actually 800 Solar charms (exactly? I must have missed something). That's surprising. That's not including MA of course. The full breakdown was:<br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Archery 32</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Athletics 30</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Awareness 22</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Brawl 49</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Bureaucracy 26</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Craft 60</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dodge 26</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Integrity 31</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Investigation 17</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Larceny 29</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Linguistics 33</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Lore 48</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Medicine 23</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Melee 38</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Occult 36</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Performance 37</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Presence 24</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Resistance 26</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Ride 36</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sail 39</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Socialize 50</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Stealth 23</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Survival 24</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Thrown 24</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">War 17</span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T13:12:24-07:00","id":1107100,"title":"","content":"Are you counting Charms from Miracles?<br /> <br /> \u200bBecause I've checked four times, and there are only 26 Archery Charms and... actually 31 Athletics Charms. Huh.<br /> <br /> \u200bStill, that probably only amounts to a minute difference. Certainly, Brawl, Craft and Socialize are large enough to throw off the average.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T13:29:34-07:00","id":1107104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1106054-dragon-blooded-charm-preview-signature-charms?p=1107100#post1107100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you counting Charms from Miracles?<br /> <br /> \u200bBecause I've checked four times, and there are only 26 Archery Charms and... actually 31 Athletics Charms. Huh.<br /> <br /> \u200bStill, that probably only amounts to a minute difference. Certainly, Brawl, Craft and Socialize are large enough to throw off the average.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not. I think I found my goof, this is a count from the Backer PDF, and there was a little tweaking since then (such as the cutting of a few Craft charms). That said, it's still closer to 800 than 600.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T13:34:42-07:00","id":1107106,"title":"","content":"3e corebook had about 793 Solar Charms based on just counting on cascades (this is excluding things like the two Charms that should have been deleted but layout didn't for whatever eason). There are also 108 Martial Arts Charms spread amongst 11 styles. So a total of about 902 Charms. This is not counting sorcery or Evocations either, which I don't feel like going through and counting due to lack of handy cascades for those :P<br /> <br /> But in that context, 125 signature Charms and maybe say, a dozen Charms per Ability still will not be much more than half the Solar Charmset. There's a lot of room for there to be hundrds of Charms and still less than Solars.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T13:50:28-07:00","id":1107112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1106054-dragon-blooded-charm-preview-signature-charms?p=1107106#post1107106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3e corebook had about 793 Solar Charms based on just counting on cascades (this is excluding things like the two Charms that should have been deleted but layout didn't for whatever eason). There are also 108 Martial Arts Charms spread amongst 11 styles. So a total of about 902 Charms. This is not counting sorcery or Evocations either, which I don't feel like going through and counting due to lack of handy cascades for those :P<br /> <br /> But in that context, 125 signature Charms and maybe say, a dozen Charms per Ability still will not be much more than half the Solar Charmset. There's a lot of room for there to be hundrds of Charms and still less than Solars.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't count the MA charms since we're just talking Native (and DB book will have it's own MA sets) so the 793 is a good comparison. <br /> <br /> Subtract the Signature charms from that and you're left with 668 charms. Divide that by 25 abilities and that leaves 26 other charms per ability if they had equal numbers to Solars. If they lowered that to 15ish and each ability had a total of 20 charms including signatures, it'd still be a lot, but less than the Solar book by almost 300.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T13:53:42-07:00","id":1107115,"title":"","content":"I tossed in MAs a bit because there are probably going to be, as I gather, less total MA styles in the book (Dragon Styles plus three more I think). Plus no Evocations, plus no base system rules and all that. That gives a lot of room for piles of DB Charms and still really robust setting info.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T14:19:56-07:00","id":1107121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1106054-dragon-blooded-charm-preview-signature-charms?p=1107115#post1107115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tossed in MAs a bit because there are probably going to be, as I gather, less total MA styles in the book (Dragon Styles plus three more I think). Plus no Evocations, plus no base system rules and all that. That gives a lot of room for piles of DB Charms and still really robust setting info.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I believe Vance said there will be some Artifacts with Evocations in the book, but all your other points are valid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T17:31:13-07:00","id":1107157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1106054-dragon-blooded-charm-preview-signature-charms?p=1107106#post1107106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3e corebook had about 793 Solar Charms based on just counting on cascades (this is excluding things like the two Charms that should have been deleted but layout didn't for whatever eason</div> </div> </div> </div>Which two are those?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T17:37:37-07:00","id":1107159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1106054-dragon-blooded-charm-preview-signature-charms?p=1107157#post1107157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which two are those?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't recall their names but they were a pair of Craft charms that reference unlocking or create Evocations with the old Emerald/Sapphire/Adamant system that was done away with before the final version of 3e. Since they were worded incompatibly they were supposed to be cut. But they somehow snuck through the editing, so they're just useless charms now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T20:24:18-07:00","id":1107194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1106054-dragon-blooded-charm-preview-signature-charms?p=1107157#post1107157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which two are those?</div> </div> </div> </div>Holden had mentioned in other places that Design Beyond Limit was originally going to be cut, plus any Charms based on it. They got kept in in part because an editing note didn't get implemented apparently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T21:55:59-07:00","id":1107207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1106054-dragon-blooded-charm-preview-signature-charms?p=1107106#post1107106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3e corebook had about 793 Solar Charms based on just counting on cascades (this is excluding things like the two Charms that should have been deleted but layout didn't for whatever eason). There are also 108 Martial Arts Charms spread amongst 11 styles. So a total of about 902 Charms. This is not counting sorcery or Evocations either, which I don't feel like going through and counting due to lack of handy cascades for those</div> </div> </div> </div>Sweet sassy molassy.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T06:44:08-07:00","id":1107295,"title":"","content":"IIRC is was mostly an attempt to avoid the problem last edition where solars had their charms spread throughout dozens of books. They wanted to try and put as many as possible in the core to avoid this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T10:05:22-07:00","id":1107346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1106054-dragon-blooded-charm-preview-signature-charms?p=1107295#post1107295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IIRC is was mostly an attempt to avoid the problem last edition where solars had their charms spread throughout dozens of books. They wanted to try and put as many as possible in the core to avoid this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. I think some of the size of Exalted 3e is that a lot of content in it would have been &quot;expansion material&quot;, such as the total volume of MAs and such. Though that said, had it been a lter OPP KS, a good amount of those things might very well have been in a spill-over book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T10:06:14-07:00","id":1107348,"title":"","content":"Just for comparison of finished First Edition Solars trees (Wordman's: <a href=\"https://thor.divnull.com/pub/exalted/charmtrees-20060324.pdf):\" target=\"_blank\">https://thor.divnull.com/pub/exalted...20060324.pdf):</a><br /> <br /> Archery: 15<br /> Athletics: 18<br /> Awareness: 14<br /> Brawl: 19<br /> Bureaucracy: 11<br /> Craft: 14<br /> Dodge: 6<br /> Endurance: 15<br /> Investigation: 10<br /> Larceny: 10<br /> Linguistics: 15<br /> Lore: 15<br /> Medicine: 16<br /> Melee: 28<br /> Occult: 13<br /> Performance: 20<br /> Presence: 14<br /> Resistance: 20<br /> Ride: 12<br /> Sail: 17<br /> Socialize: 14<br /> Stealth: 7<br /> Survival: 17<br /> Thrown: 13<br /> <br /> -----<br /> Total: 353<br /> ---<br /> <br /> That's still a lot of Charms... But 3e is about twice as many. They worked hard.<br /> <br /> (Also: back when I did a quick exercise in another thread this year to test whether 3e Charms were wordier than 2e and Infernals, median wordcount per Charm seemed about the same between 3e and 2e, while Infernals was about 20% longer per Charm).<br /> <br /> Comparably Dragonblooded have 250, in non-MA Ability cascades, from all material.<br /> *edit Sidereal - 148.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":929,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","user":"Ghosthead","date":". 06-24-2017, 01:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T11:46:36-07:00","id":1107388,"title":"","content":"Really, considering what they said in the Kickstarter preview about how being in charge means that they get to decide how many Charms can be assigned to differentiate elements, I think there's far less getting away from a sizable Charm chapter for Dragon Blooded than there ever was for Solars.<br /> <br /> \u200bHopefully, for your people who found the Solar Charms chapter to be a bit impenetrable, the level of variation in form and organisation inherent to the elemental qualities might draw the eye a bit more.<br /> <br /> \u200bI'm sure I will be, and I <i>like</i> the Solar Charms chapter.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe book as a whole... well, compared to the core, there are definitely a lot of things that can be cut down, although I'm also interested in seeing what level of detail that they can give to the Houses when the overall Realm information is being consolidated in its own book.<br /> <br /> \u200b...I can't recall, did they say that the Houses would be in the Realm book, or the Exalted one?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T13:34:22-07:00","id":1107408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1106054-dragon-blooded-charm-preview-signature-charms?p=1107388#post1107388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b...I can't recall, did they say that the Houses would be in the Realm book, or the Exalted one?</div> </div> </div> </div>...probably both of them? Like I can't imagine a DB book that doesn't talk about them. But I imagine the Realm book having significantly more detail.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T15:58:06-07:00","id":1107436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1106054-dragon-blooded-charm-preview-signature-charms?p=1107408#post1107408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...probably both of them? Like I can't imagine a DB book that doesn't talk about them. But I imagine the Realm book having significantly more detail.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean if they don't mention the Major DB Families in the DB book... Well while the Dynastic Houses will have greater detail in the Realm book, people who wanna play Lookshyans would be SOL if there's no writeup of Lookshy and the Gentes in WFHW","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T16:40:35-07:00","id":1107445,"title":"","content":"I checked the blurbs of both books, and the one for The Realm is the one that says &quot;a large part of this book will be devoted to detailing the houses of the Dynasty, updating and enlivening with intention of making the houses as tantalizing as Kindred Clans in terms of iconicism and player association and appeal&quot;.<br /> <br /> So that is the answer to my question, and the underlying one of whether or not What Fire Has Wrought would need to balance a large Charms chapter with an especially large collection of setting details.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T18:06:40-07:00","id":1107460,"title":"","content":"If the past is anything to go one the DB boom will describe what the houses are like generally, maybe with a few examples of key players, and the realm book will get into the gritty details of how they operate and where and their interactions with each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T02:34:30-07:00","id":1107587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1106054-dragon-blooded-charm-preview-signature-charms?p=1107445#post1107445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I checked the blurbs of both books, and the one for The Realm is the one that says &quot;a large part of this book will be devoted to detailing the houses of the Dynasty, updating and enlivening with intention of making the houses as tantalizing as Kindred Clans in terms of iconicism and player association and appeal&quot;.<br /> <br /> So that is the answer to my question, and the underlying one of whether or not What Fire Has Wrought would need to balance a large Charms chapter with an especially large collection of setting details.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I guess that doesn't mean the Houses won't be talked about at all in the DB book, but it does sound like it'll probably be less.<br /> <br /> Which is maybe fine, as they can talk a bit more about some different Outcaste groups.<br /> <br /> Am I remembering correctly that Vance said he thought the best thing to do with education, rather than the old system of extra ability dots but compulsory stuff, was some specialties? Like you get some free specialties if you're a Dynast, some different ones if you're from Lookshy.<br /> Because that would make me wonder if you'd get specialties from which Dynastic school you went to (as that was part of DB character gen before), and if so, I wonder if they'd talk about the schools in the DB book like they did before (I mean, that's only about 1 page).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 06-25-2017, 05:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T07:00:49-07:00","id":1107621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1106054-dragon-blooded-charm-preview-signature-charms?p=1107587#post1107587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I remembering correctly that Vance said he thought the best thing to do with education, rather than the old system of extra ability dots but compulsory stuff, was some specialties? Like you get some free specialties if you're a Dynast, some different ones if you're from Lookshy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which could mean that instead of 35 Ability dots to distribute, you could only have the same 28 available to Solar Exalted.<br /> <br /> Which would further pinch Dragon-Blooded character creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T10:38:40-07:00","id":1107679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1106054-dragon-blooded-charm-preview-signature-charms?p=1107621#post1107621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which could mean that instead of 35 Ability dots to distribute, you could only have the same 28 available to Solar Exalted.<br /> <br /> Which would further pinch Dragon-Blooded character creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I am in favor of everyone getting the same number of Ability dots. If Solars and probably Lunars get the same number of dots no matter their amount of implied-by-backstory training and education, why should DBs get more? One of the things I didn't like about 2e was how Outcastes got less dots than Realm/Lookshy DBs and Ronin Sidereals got less than Heaven-employed ones.<br /> Why should some of the splats get &quot;optimize your backstory for more dots&quot; as a thing?<br /> <br /> &quot;I'm Prince Diamond, a scion of warrior nobility that ruled my land of origin. My incredibly rich family has hired the best teachers money can buy to educate me in a wide variety of subjects. Since then, I have also become a far-rider, traveling far and wide and experiencing a myriad of cultures&quot;. 28 dots<br /> <br /> &quot;Hey, I'm 6\u00ba Daughter, I was a simple mud-farming child in a poor village in the middle of nowhere. When I couldn't stand father beating mom anymore, I was ready to die to protect her, but instead the Sun chose to smile upon a poor kid like me that day&quot;. Also 28 dots<br /> <br /> &quot;My Name is, or was, Mnemon Karagi. I have been considered something of a prodigy and have learned the ways of Sorcery while still a young mortal. As such, there was much expectation that I would be chosen by the Dragons, and my family kept investing in me even when that turned unreasonable. I was past my 25th year when they accepted that Exaltation was not in my destiny. Or so they thought. The mark of Twilight now shines in my brow. That dotting family of mine now sees me as a monster, a final failure of their once promising prodigy, but I know otherwise.&quot; 28 dots as well.<br /> <br /> If playing a Solar character you must portray &quot;expensively educated, well-traveled warrior nobility&quot; as well as &quot;mud-farming, bully-stopping child who has never seen beyond the hill closest to the village&quot; and &quot;prodigious <i>Dynastic scion </i>with all the education, training and expectations that implies&quot;, using the same amount of Ability dots, what is the justification for any splat getting more? I doubt it would be mechanical balance, since some extra Ability dots are unlikely to put a DB and, say, a Lunar, on equal footing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T10:56:42-07:00","id":1107686,"title":"","content":"I have a certain attachment to the older systems of Dragon Blooded character creation, but it's an insignificant hill to die on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T12:21:08-07:00","id":1107708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1106054-dragon-blooded-charm-preview-signature-charms?p=1107388#post1107388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b...I can't recall, did they say that the Houses would be in the Realm book, or the Exalted one?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Great Houses are discussed in detail in <i>Dragon-Blooded</i>, since detailed information on the Houses is important to designing and playing Dragon-Blooded PCs and NPCs. <i>The Realm</i> just has a basic outline of the houses and their situation, so you have context if you're using the book without also owning <i>Dragon-Blooded</i> (such as for a mortals game set on the Blessed Isle, or a Solar game set in a satrapy).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T12:26:03-07:00","id":1107710,"title":"","content":"reversal of what was stated in blurbs. fine","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T12:26:28-07:00","id":1107711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1106054-dragon-blooded-charm-preview-signature-charms?p=1107679#post1107679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I am in favor of everyone getting the same number of Ability dots.</div> </div> </div> </div>Me, too.<br /> <br /> Didn't mean to convey that I wasn't. I would sooner give Dragon-Blooded a bit more flexibility with their Aspect Abilities than give them more dots.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T12:58:59-07:00","id":1107722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1106054-dragon-blooded-charm-preview-signature-charms?p=1107679#post1107679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If playing a Solar character you must portray &quot;expensively educated, well-traveled warrior nobility&quot; as well as &quot;mud-farming, bully-stopping child who has never seen beyond the hill closest to the village&quot; and &quot;prodigious <i>Dynastic scion </i>with all the education, training and expectations that implies&quot;, using the same amount of Ability dots, what is the justification for any splat getting more? I doubt it would be mechanical balance, since some extra Ability dots are unlikely to put a DB and, say, a Lunar, on equal footing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not between splat balance, but well, it's intra-Solar player balance within group, between people who wish to play twelve year old boy, and those that wish to play Admiral Sand. The idea here, I would guess, being that someone who wants to play a Solar with a simple background should not be disadvantaged to another player in their group who picks a fancy background.<br /> <br /> Not an issue with Dragonblooded Dynast games, where they come from a shared cultural context and PCs are assumed to Exalt around the same age, so the assumed level of dots can be placed higher.<br /> <br /> If 28 dots is enough for young Dynasts to be as skilled as they are supposed to play as, then no problem with setting it that way. But if not, I wouldn't really see the point of restricting their chargen and providing a qualitatively worse Dynast experience in order to for feels of symmetry with some distant convention that exists to make Solar games fairer between players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T13:17:00-07:00","id":1107730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1106054-dragon-blooded-charm-preview-signature-charms?p=1107679#post1107679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Personally, I am in favor of everyone getting the same number of Ability dots. If Solars and probably Lunars get the same number of dots no matter their amount of implied-by-backstory training and education, why should DBs get more? One of the things I didn't like about 2e was how Outcastes got less dots than Realm/Lookshy DBs and Ronin Sidereals got less than Heaven-employed ones.<br /> Why should some of the splats get &quot;optimize your backstory for more dots&quot; as a thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm happy for DBs to have the same amount of ability dots as Solars, if they also have the same amount of attributes.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't mind them having more merits, but with 10, it's not really necessary.<br /> <br /> I'm not really sure vis-a-vis charms though. Maybe they ought to have the same as Solars (ie 15) because they don't get free excellencies anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T14:05:32-07:00","id":1107759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1106054-dragon-blooded-charm-preview-signature-charms?p=1107730#post1107730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm happy for DBs to have the same amount of ability dots as Solars, if they also have the same amount of attributes.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't mind them having more merits, but with 10, it's not really necessary.<br /> <br /> I'm not really sure vis-a-vis charms though. Maybe they ought to have the same as Solars (ie 15) because they don't get free excellencies anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually I think 10 might be cutting it close. If you want to build an average dynast you have veeeery little wiggle room there once you get your resources and stuff sorted out.<br /> <br /> Without free excellencies they might want more charms than you would think, but I heard their excellency replacements are interesting enough to warrant a purchase.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T14:26:44-07:00","id":1107763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1106054-dragon-blooded-charm-preview-signature-charms?p=1107759#post1107759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually I think 10 might be cutting it close. If you want to build an average dynast you have veeeery little wiggle room there once you get your resources and stuff sorted out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dynasts should not need to have the Resources Merit by default.<br /> <br /> \u200bYou can easily play somebody with the lifestyle of a Dynast who either lives off of social association with others, earns money without consistency and spends it immediately, or is perpetually in debt.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat's something that has been common to a subset of rich people throughout history; they don't necessarily go broke the way that poor people do.<br /> <br /> \u200b(I think most people probably don't want to play an average Dynast, because an average Dynast is about a century old, and has job and family commitments. I think most people want to play a Dynast who is younger than about sixty, who is still alternately working on all of the interesting things necessary to establish a firm base and be eligible as a marriage prospect, and going out to have fun adventures.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T15:31:52-07:00","id":1107777,"title":"","content":"Yeah, PCs are understood to be exceptional by the standards of whatever they are. For example, the book says most exalts never hit essence 5, but a PC is totally expected to. They are the movers and shakers of Creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T16:26:49-07:00","id":1107790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1106054-dragon-blooded-charm-preview-signature-charms?p=1107763#post1107763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dynasts should not need to have the Resources Merit by default.<br /> <br /> \u200bYou can easily play somebody with the lifestyle of a Dynast who either lives off of social association with others, earns money without consistency and spends it immediately, or is perpetually in debt.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat's something that has been common to a subset of rich people throughout history; they don't necessarily go broke the way that poor people do.<br /> <br /> \u200b(I think most people probably don't want to play an average Dynast, because an average Dynast is about a century old, and has job and family commitments. I think most people want to play a Dynast who is younger than about sixty, who is still alternately working on all of the interesting things necessary to establish a firm base and be eligible as a marriage prospect, and going out to have fun adventures.)</div> </div> </div> </div>That's very true indeed, but a dynast with no breeding, contacts, influence, reputation, resources, artifacts, command, backing etc. starts to make less sense. You can totally do it, and that's a legitimate character, I mean I'm playing a Dawn with only one dot of combat ability and it's not even in his supernal, but even for your average PC dynast I think it's a bit strange.<br /> <br /> Those other merits are how one lives it up while being in crushing debt, and I think it's a good thing if DB character gen makes that easier to accomplish. It's also a great way to give you the feeling of absolutely enormous privilege that being a scion of the most bloody, oppressive and grand empire in the world affords you. Like if you personally feel like you can just take a dot or two of retainers on a whim, that's what being a dynast feels like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T16:38:18-07:00","id":1107797,"title":"","content":"*finally got around to reading the preview*<br /> <br /> God dammit. I knew a Fire DB Sorceress (Pact with an Ifrit Lord) was gonna be powerful and I felt like maybe I was pushing it a bit. But <i>this</i>? You can't expect me to withold Wildfire-Taming Technique from her.<br /> <br /> My players are so screwed. I love it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T17:30:48-07:00","id":1107823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1106054-dragon-blooded-charm-preview-signature-charms?p=1107790#post1107790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's very true indeed, but a dynast with no breeding, contacts, influence, reputation, resources, artifacts, command, backing etc. starts to make less sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI think that between how many dots there are at character creation and what is offered by most of the Merits that are not any of those, that one doesn't need to worry too much about somebody struggling between a Dynast who makes sense and the ambidextrous, fleet-footed danger-senser with the unbendable stomach that their heart was set on.<br /> <br /> \u200b...Actually, scratch that facetiousness; somebody with those qualities seems perfectly cromulent as an expression on a Dynast who places far more emphasis on adventures in the Threshold than high society.<br /> <br /> \u200b(Also, all but one of those Merits can be acquired in the course of the story, so one way or another it doesn't need to be a shortcoming that lasts for very long)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T20:47:27-07:00","id":1107871,"title":"","content":"@Isator_Levi and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1121_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1121\" data-vbnamecard=\"1121\">DrLoveMonkey</a>, I think we might get two or three more merit dots, but if dragon-blooded get the same number of BP as Solar's then the difference in what a merits DB society demand the character can purchase using free ranks can easily be bought up using BP.<br /> <br /> The way I see it, the average Dynast about the same age as a starting character will look like this:<br /> <br /> Job (Backing/Command/Sorcery): 3<br /> Social Status (Breeding/Influence/Contacts): 3<br /> Gear (Artifacts/Demanse/Manse/Hearthstone): 3<br /> Language: 1<br /> Resources:3<br /> <br /> So without the extra free ranks of merits, it would take an investment of 3 BP to get this result (and that's not unreasonable). <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1g_IC644YJoiVAm6ngqcBmsQtff2YYtd3pDbZpaOxx4o\" target=\"_blank\">My Exalted Character Creation Tool may be downloaded here.</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1086797-demac-s-exalted-character-creation-tool\" target=\"_blank\">The thread talking about the tool can be found here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1136654-exalted-seats-of-power\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted: Seats of Power is a homebrewed manse creation system.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1oaq3wk7lJKZ022SUA4iPfGzMpmBTNXlM\" target=\"_blank\">I have a rewrite of the craft system which can be downloaded here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1070312-i-got-my-book-it-s-super-fancy-and-i-can-t-read-the-cover/page2\" target=\"_blank\">I like the Mesoamerican look</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2346-demac","name":"Demac","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T01:51:12-07:00","id":1107944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1106054-dragon-blooded-charm-preview-signature-charms?p=1107823#post1107823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bI think that between how many dots there are at character creation and what is offered by most of the Merits that are not any of those, that one doesn't need to worry too much about somebody struggling between a Dynast who makes sense and the ambidextrous, fleet-footed danger-senser with the unbendable stomach that their heart was set on.<br /> <br /> \u200b...Actually, scratch that facetiousness; somebody with those qualities seems perfectly cromulent as an expression on a Dynast who places far more emphasis on adventures in the Threshold than high society.<br /> <br /> \u200b(Also, all but one of those Merits can be acquired in the course of the story, so one way or another it doesn't need to be a shortcoming that lasts for very long)</div> </div> </div> </div>That sort of takes away from the flavour of that kind of character though, doesn't it? If you're playing somebody who starts the game with artifact armour, weapon, hearthstone and is ambidexterous you very pointedly have zero breeding, no backing from your house, no influence, no important contacts or personal wealth. That's actually a very interesting character, because they have basically zero support from their family, and the empire as a whole.<br /> <br /> It also kind of jabs the guy who actually spent all his merits and half his BP on social standing, wealth and contacts if they're not aquired so easily. They're not things you just automatically get as a dynast, and I would never allow the concept of say, a Threshold king to be a PC without investing pretty heavily into those merits<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1106054-dragon-blooded-charm-preview-signature-charms?p=1107871#post1107871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way I see it, the average Dynast about the same age as a starting character will look like this:<br /> <br /> Job (Backing/Command/Sorcery): 3<br /> Social Status (Breeding/Influence/Contacts): 3<br /> Gear (Artifacts/Demanse/Manse/Hearthstone): 3<br /> Language: 1<br /> Resources:3<br /> <br /> So without the extra free ranks of merits, it would take an investment of 3 BP to get this result (and that's not unreasonable). </div> </div> </div> </div>I do think that extra three dots would be a good thing though. There are incredible, incredible advantages to being a scion of the great houses and I just feel that should be represented.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T02:46:29-07:00","id":1107954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1106054-dragon-blooded-charm-preview-signature-charms?p=1107944#post1107944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That sort of takes away from the flavour of that kind of character though, doesn't it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel as though you're responding to a specific part of my post, but I can't tell because you've quoted the whole thing, to which I can't really make sense of this as a response.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're playing somebody who starts the game with artifact armour, weapon, hearthstone</div> </div> </div> </div>If your point is &quot;it being possible to acquire Story Merits in the story makes them a poor choice at character creation&quot;, I would say that the point of taking them at character creation is something between them being essential to the character, wanting to take advantage of them right out of the gate, and being very uninterested in playing through the stories of acquiring them. I think those things are all substantial enough to validate Story Merits as character creation purchases.<br /> <br /> \u200bTo be sure, even accounting for the option to calibrate further by bonus points that Demac pointed out, there are ultimately going to be character concepts that are a bit beyond what can be constructed from the outset, to which I say that some reasonable limitations are just something that some players will have to deal with.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would never allow the concept of say, a Threshold king to be a PC without investing pretty heavily into those merits</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWhy not? There have been numerous monarchs throughout history who had very little actual wealth and power, constantly undermined by a virtually independent aristocracy, who had not yet declared themselves kings either out of inertia, cultural values that would have been averse to such usurpation, or simply finding king to be a step down from the power and privilege that they enjoyed in the moment.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T11:08:20-07:00","id":1108080,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry I'm touring around Scotland at the moment, it's making it hard to find a computer to perform piecewise quotes.<br /> <br /> I was basically saying that making it easy to quickly attain those merits in short order it makes it kind of flavourless to pick a character that pointedly doesn't have them, which would make him a rare dynasty indeed and a great PC. <br /> <br /> But maybe I'm going about this the wrong way. Isator what would YOU do to differentiate Dynastic character generation to show that you are creating a member of the absolute most powerful* and privileged class of people in the entire world? Because I agree that bonus ability dots are a bad way, since it's so easy for any character to have a backstory with that kind of training, particulatly with the mentor merit. <br /> <br /> I would say the same for sidereals as well, unless they're ronin.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;\u200bWhy not? There have been numerous monarchs throughout history who had very little actual wealth and power, constantly undermined by a virtually independent aristocracy, who had not yet declared themselves kings either out of inertia, cultural values that would have been averse to such usurpation, or simply finding king to be a step down from the power and privilege that they enjoyed in the moment.&quot;<br /> <br /> *head desk* now I remember why I stopped posting on this forum. Okay in that instance absolutely. But in most cases when one references a threshold king they mean somebody with at least a modicum of power. Not somebody who is so divorced from his military, family, guards, and aristocracy as to have little to no ability to drawn on or affect any of it.<br /> <br /> Sometimes I swear if I said I vetoed the concept of playing a kryptonian in a mortal hero game somebody would criticize me for disallowing the concept of a molecule chamber de-powered superman.<br /> <br /> *politically powerful anyway","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T20:08:47-07:00","id":1108245,"title":"","content":"Here's my thing: I like the fact that there's not going to be tiered PC character creation rules. If a player wants to play a dynast, they can dump their bonus points into their merits to reflect their background. Ultimately, characters with many merits aren't choosing them at the expense of other merits. They're choosing them at the expense of other traits or charms. And to me, that's a legitimate choice to make on several levels. There are some real advantages to choosing to play a merit master vs. a skill master, but at the same time, you're also choosing to play a character who chose to work on increasing his social standing rather than raising 7 different abilities to rank 5. So it's a trade off.<br /> <br /> Like I said, I can see that in Creation, Dragon-Blooded (and I mean all Dragon-Blooded) have some inherent benefits in building their influence due to the prevalence of the immaculate philosophy and their ability to flare their anima without fear of being the object of a Wyld Hunt, but beyond a few dots over other splats, I wouldn't think a specific subset of Dragon-Blooded would get preference over others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1g_IC644YJoiVAm6ngqcBmsQtff2YYtd3pDbZpaOxx4o\" target=\"_blank\">My Exalted Character Creation Tool may be downloaded here.</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1086797-demac-s-exalted-character-creation-tool\" target=\"_blank\">The thread talking about the tool can be found here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1136654-exalted-seats-of-power\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted: Seats of Power is a homebrewed manse creation system.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1oaq3wk7lJKZ022SUA4iPfGzMpmBTNXlM\" target=\"_blank\">I have a rewrite of the craft system which can be downloaded here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1070312-i-got-my-book-it-s-super-fancy-and-i-can-t-read-the-cover/page2\" target=\"_blank\">I like the Mesoamerican look</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2346-demac","name":"Demac","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}